      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "@Dasha Andriyenko \n\nOption 3 looks like what we currently have.\n\nI think both options 1 and 2 are an improvement.\n\nOption 2 is very easy to implement, since it is so similar to option 3, just with different strings. \n\nOption 1 probably feels best, but we would need to choose an ultimate fallback language for the target in case we absolutely cannot determine anything else.\n\nWe've had to do this in the past for SelectTranslationsPanel, falling back to English as a last resort. \n\nThis would only ever happen if the user has never translated before, and none of their web requested languages or UI language are a valid option for translation. Very rare these days, since we support so many more languages than at the start.\n\nMy vote is for option 1.\n\nThis also lessens the burden of getting started. The user can just start typing, where as with the setup in options 2 and 3 they have to open the dropdown and select a target.",
      "reactions": [],
